  "added_test_names": [
    "copies a complete tab with fresh field identities, internal formulas and visibility rules while retaining external references",
    "remaps organization, date, source filters and mapping targets across copied siblings",
    "copies subform columns together, omits serial fields and leaves existing records and published snapshots unchanged",
    "removes only the tab and returns its fields in their original order without changing identities, rules or values",
    "reorders persisted tabs without rewriting field order, identity or data",
    "enforces 2–50 on remove, add and copy without partial changes, including stale confirmations",
    "adds an empty tab at the end and can copy an empty tab at the field limit",
    "counts tab children but not tab containers, and rejects a copy beyond 300 atomically",
    "loads old single-tab and nested layouts without silently changing them; copying cannot create another nested tabs field",
    "keeps one main tabs field across add, duplicate, drop and restore; ordinary fields may still be added inside it",
    "allows 300 real fields plus one tabs container consistently on add and trash restore",
    "moves a field into a tab with more than 150 children instead of silently ignoring the drop",
    "cancels deletion using Escape, outside click and Cancel without changing the schema",
    "confirms deletion in one undoable change and restores the exact fields, tabs and rules on undo/redo",
    "selects the copied tab on the canvas and puts the next dragged/click-added field in that tab",
    "supports keyboard reorder with the same saved and runtime order, without treating rename keystrokes as drag commands",
    "disables both add/copy at 50 and deletion at 2, while allowing copy of a populated tab"
  ],
